Hello all, here's the plan for the holiday trip, including who drives which d=
ay.

The village fete is next Saturday. There will be the usual cake stall and dog=
 show, and I have somehow been talked into helping with the tombola.

We are thinking of a short trip to the coast next month. Nothing fancy, just =
a couple of nights somewhere quiet with a good walk and a decent place for fi=
sh and chips.

The fox has been visiting the garden again. We see it most evenings just afte=
r dark, trotting along the fence and stopping to look at the house before it =
goes.

We are looking forward to seeing you at the end of the month. The spare bed i=
s made up, and I have found the board game we used to play, so be ready for a=
 rematch.

The school play was a great success. The children had clearly practised for w=
eeks, and the costumes were remarkable considering most of them were made fro=
m old curtains.

We have been clearing out the loft and found a box of old letters from Grandm=
a. Some of them are very funny, and I will bring a few along for you to read.

The repairs to the roof are done at last. The builders were tidy and quick on=
ce they started, and we no longer need the bucket in the attic when it rains.

Thank you again for the recipe. I made the soup on Sunday and everyone went b=
ack for seconds, even my brother, who usually refuses anything with lentils i=
n it.

The swimming lessons are going well. Our youngest can now manage a length wit=
hout the float, and she is very proud of the certificate she brought home.

I bumped into your cousin at the station last week. She looked well and asked=
 to be remembered to you; she is still working at the library and seems to en=
joy it.

The dog has been enjoying the cooler mornings. We have started walking the lo=
ng way round the lake, and she always stops to say hello to the ducks by the =
old boathouse.

The local library has started a repair cafe once a month. I took the old lamp=
 along, and a retired electrician had it working again within twenty minutes.

Could you take the second day's drive and pick up Gran on the way?

--=20
Tom

